WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.090
A new food truck parks outside a ballpark.

2
00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:05.630
It sells out before the game is over.

3
00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:09.110
Its price is far above
its average total cost.

4
00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:11.780
The owner earns an economic profit.

5
00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:14.670
A few years later, the
truck is still busy.

6
00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:17.660
But its economic profit
has fallen to zero.

7
00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:20.780
Same truck, same food, still busy.

8
00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.920
So where did the profit go?

9
00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:25.620
In this mission, you'll
find the price and quantity

10
00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:27.970
that maximize this firm's profit.

11
00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:30.620
Then you'll change the
market in a graph lab,

12
00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:33.670
and predict where each firm
ends up in the long run.

13
00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:36.940
Your mission: find out
why a big profit at first

14
00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:40.360
can shrink to zero, even
when customers keep coming.
